Z||000000||Pheagey||12-06-2001||06:02 PM||||Please ewxcuss my ignorance for I know little about trannies/clutched.<BR>   1)Is it possible to mate a Porche 6 speed tranny/clutch to a 350?<BR>   2)Is it possible for that tranny to have two clutch plates?<BR>   3)Can that same tranny have racing low gears (4.1-1 I beleive) and cruising higher gears (3.2-1, again I beleive)?<P>Ok, that anof my my babling<P>------------------<BR>'88 coupe, 5 speed, custome paint job<BR>"I! have a plan!"<BR>Have you seen my website yet?<BR>Http://www.LithiumEffects/pheageysfeiro<BR>Killed: '97 civic CS auto;<BR>Killed by: '94 Civic Ex, '96 Camery LX<BR>Vandalised: 2 time (in 2 days).||||reg||5
Z||000001||Turbo88||12-06-2001||06:11 PM||||No question is a stupid one! <P>1. Yes, you can. I forget the name of the company that makes the adapter but someone at Ryane Motorsports told me who they are. Ryane (now Held), should be able to point you in the proper direction. <A HREF="http://www.heldmotorsports.com" TARGET=_blank>www.heldmotorsports.com</A>  <P>2. I don't see why not if you have someone make you one. Multistage clutches are not totally rare but why would you want one? If you mean can you put two clutches together? You can't do that.<P>3. I don't see why you can't regear your final drive but you have to find someone who sells or can custom make you the gears.<P>Hope this helps..||||reg||1
Z||000002||avengador1||12-06-2001||06:13 PM||||I have heard of Porsche trannies being mated to 350 engines before. You need an adapter plate of course. As for multiple clutch discs, I have only seen these in drag race cars. Pick up a kit car mag and you might find info on the trans adapter plates there. Hope this helps. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">I'll try to look thru mine to see if I find something and post it later.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Avendgador1.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000003||Phil||12-06-2001||07:19 PM||||Seem to remember a place called Renegade -something-Motor Sports I think that did Porsche tranny conversion for Fiero based kit cars.||||reg||1
